Fix fatal error: RdfParsingTrait::assertSession() incompatible with KernelTestBase

Drupal core added Drupal\Tests\HttpKernelUiHelperTrait to KernelTestBase
(https://www.drupal.org/project/drupal/issues/3390193 and
https://www.drupal.org/node/3502609, "Kernel tests can make HTTP requests
with drupalGet()"), which declares a typed
assertSession($name = NULL): Drupal\Tests\WebAssert.

RdfParsingTrait (used by both functional tests, extending BrowserTestBase,
and the "rdf" module's own FieldRdfaTestBase kernel test base, extending
KernelTestBase) hard-codes `use Drupal\Tests\UiHelperTrait;`, whose
assertSession($name = NULL) has no return type. When composed into a
KernelTestBase descendant, PHP fatals:

  Fatal error: Declaration of Drupal\Tests\rdf\Traits\RdfParsingTrait::
  assertSession($name = null) must be compatible with
  Drupal\KernelTests\KernelTestBase::assertSession($name = null):
  Drupal\Tests\WebAssert

This fatal is thrown during PHPUnit's Drupal test-suite discovery (which
parses every test class across all modules to read @group annotations
before any --group filtering happens), so it breaks the entire test run,
not just RDF-specific tests.

RdfParsingTrait's own methods only rely on $this->drupalGet(), which every
current consumer already inherits from its own parent test base class:
BrowserTestBase provides UiHelperTrait (functional tests), and
KernelTestBase now provides the compatible HttpKernelUiHelperTrait (kernel
tests). Removing the trait's redundant `use UiHelperTrait;` resolves the
conflict without any loss of functionality.

No newer 3.x release of drupal/rdf exists (3.0.0-beta2 is the latest, and
this file is unchanged on the 3.0.x branch HEAD as of this writing); 4.0.0
requires drupal/core ^11.3 and is not usable while on Drupal 10.

--- a/tests/src/Traits/RdfParsingTrait.php
+++ b/tests/src/Traits/RdfParsingTrait.php
@@ -3,7 +3,6 @@
 namespace Drupal\Tests\rdf\Traits;

 use Drupal\Core\Url;
-use Drupal\Tests\UiHelperTrait;
 use EasyRdf\Graph;
 use EasyRdf\Parser\Rdfa;

@@ -12,8 +11,6 @@
  */
 trait RdfParsingTrait {

-  use UiHelperTrait;
-
   /**
    * Checks if a html document contains a resource with a given property value.
    *
